<title>FRANCE: U.S. top destination for Paris Dec 96 exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top destination for Paris Dec 96 exports.</headline>
<text>
<p>PARIS, Feb 19 (Reuter) The United States was the principal destination for exports handled at the Paris airports in</p>
<p>December 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris</p>
<p>(ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 leading destinations by country for exports in tonnes</p>
<p>in December 1996, with percentage change on December 1995, were:</p>
<p> 1  United States	     10,999   up    18.4pct</p>
<p> 2  Japan			  2,303   down  17.1</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong		    1,966   down  8.3</p>
<p> 4  United Kingdom	     1,757   up   77.4</p>
<p> 5  Germany			1,701   up   38.6</p>
<p> 6  Canada			 1,473   down 21.9</p>
<p> 7  French West Indies	 1,462   up    6.4</p>
<p> 8  Brazil			 1,321   down  8.3</p>
<p> 9  Mexico			 1,251   up   58.5</p>
<p> 10 Reunion			1,146   up   13.3</p>
<p> 11 United Arab Emirates     1,098   up   17.7</p>
<p> 12 Singapore		    1,090   up   70.6</p>
<p> 13 India			  1,089   down 22.6</p>
<p> 14 Saudi Arabia		   935   up    5.2</p>
<p> 15 Italy			    831   up   21.2</p>
<p> 16 China			    795   down 25.7</p>
<p> 17 Korea			    793   up   22.4</p>
<p> 18 Egypt			    769   up    9.0</p>
<p> 19 Lebanon			  691   up   17.4</p>
<p> 20 Thailand			 548   down 10.0</p>
<p>    Total			 34,018</p>
<p>    Global export traffic   50,786   up    7.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
